# Legacy WordPress redirects.
#
# Verified directly against the live site (https://goodsecretssafaris.com)
# on 2026-08-26 - fetched its actual navigation and homepage content and
# compared every slug it links to against this repo's current seed data,
# rather than assuming old and new slugs line up.
#
# /about-2 and /contact-2 are simple, fixed 1:1 mappings - low risk.
#
# /accommodation-packag/* used to be a single wildcard rule
# (/hotels/:splat) on the assumption that every old hotel slug matches
# the new one exactly. That's true for 7 of the 8 hotels currently on
# the live site, but NOT for PrideInn Paradise Beach Resort & Spa: the
# legacy slug is "prideinn-paradise-beach-resort-spa", the new one is
# "prideinn-paradise-beach-resort" (no "-spa"). The wildcard would have
# 301'd that one straight to a 404. Replaced with explicit per-hotel
# rules instead, matching this project's own documented migration
# process (docs/migration/README.md: "Build redirect-map.csv with one
# row per valuable legacy URL"), which a broad wildcard skipped.
#
# IMPORTANT - NOT covered here, and NOT safe to cover with a wildcard:
# individual tour pages (legacy /safari-tour-packages/:slug/) and
# destination pages (legacy /destination/:slug/). Checked several
# examples directly against the live site and slugs were extensively
# renamed during the rebuild - e.g. legacy
# "masai-mara-national-reserve" vs this site's "maasai-mara", legacy
# "14-day-ultimate-kenya-tanzania-safari-experience" vs this site's
# "14-day-ultimate-kenya-tanzania-safari". A wildcard here would send
# most visitors and search crawlers to 404s, not the intended page.
# These need the full discover -> build redirect-map.csv -> validate
# workflow already documented in docs/migration/README.md and
# docs/launch/seo-migration-checklist.md before they can be added
# safely - do not add a tours/* or destination/* wildcard without that.
#
# Also note: the legacy site's main tour-listing link (in its own
# current navigation) is /safari-tour-packages/, not
# /all-tours-and-safaris - kept the existing /all-tours-and-safaris
# rule in case it's a real, older, unindexed slug, and added the
# actual current one alongside it.

